## Dependency injection (Registry)

Follow **[docs/front-end/dependency-injection.md](../../../docs/front-end/dependency-injection.md)**.

- **ViewModels** resolve `Service`, query keys, and `queryClient` **only** via `Registry.getInstance().inject(...)` — do **not** pass these through the binder/props tree.
- **Services** and adapters (`IHttpClient`, repositories) take dependencies in the **constructor**; **`App.tsx`** (or bootstrap) builds `new Service(...)` and **`register`**s instances.
- **Do not** `jest.mock` the Registry module in tests — use `clear()` + `register()` (see [tests.md](../../../docs/front-end/tests.md)).
- **Do not** use field decorators / `@Inject` — composition lives in bootstrap only.

Reference: [dependency-injection.md](../../../docs/front-end/dependency-injection.md) · [architecture.md](../../../docs/front-end/architecture.md)
